          "hint": "Add a filter under body.colorblind .scene and toggle the 'colorblind' class on <body>.",
          "starter": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<style>\nbody { font-family: system-ui; padding: 20px; }\n  .scene { display: flex; gap: 10px; padding: 16px; border-radius: 12px; }\n  .chip { width: 90px; height: 90px; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .c1 { background: #e03a3a; } .c2 { background: #3a8ae0; }\n  .c3 { background: #3ad8a6; } .c4 { background: #e8b83a; }\n  /* Add a filter (e.g. on body.colorblind .scene) that simulates color\n     blindness when the class is on <body>. */\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<button id=\"toggle\">Simulate color blindness</button>\n  <div class=\"scene\">\n    <div class=\"chip c1\"></div><div class=\"chip c2\"></div>\n    <div class=\"chip c3\"></div><div class=\"chip c4\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n<script>\n// Toggle the \"colorblind\" class on <body> when the button is clicked.\n\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
          "solution": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<style>\nbody { font-family: system-ui; padding: 20px; }\n  .scene { display: flex; gap: 10px; padding: 16px; border-radius: 12px; }\n  .chip { width: 90px; height: 90px; border-radius: 10px; }\n  .c1 { background: #e03a3a; } .c2 { background: #3a8ae0; }\n  .c3 { background: #3ad8a6; } .c4 { background: #e8b83a; }\n  body.colorblind .scene { filter: saturate(8%); }\n\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<button id=\"toggle\">Simulate color blindness</button>\n  <div class=\"scene\">\n    <div class=\"chip c1\"></div><div class=\"chip c2\"></div>\n    <div class=\"chip c3\"></div><div class=\"chip c4\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n<script>\n// Toggle the \"colorblind\" class on <body> when the button is clicked.\n\ndocument.getElementById(\"toggle\").addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n  document.body.classList.toggle(\"colorblind\");\n});\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
